# UI Primitives (`src/ui/`)

Thin Radix + Tailwind wrappers. Owned source — shadcn fork, not an npm package.

## Allowed

- Styling via `cn()` and CVA variants
- Small prop extensions (e.g. `fullWidth` on `PopoverContent`)
- `'use client'` when using Radix hooks/state
- Compound sub-components (`DialogHeader`, `CommandItem`, …)

## Not allowed

- Business logic, API calls, app i18n strings
- Label, hint, error UI (belongs in `components/`)
- Complex controlled state (multi-select logic, pagination)
- Import from `@/components/`

## Add a primitive

```bash
npm run ui:add -- dialog
```

After CLI: verify `@/lib/utils` imports, `new-york` style, avoid overwriting intentional customizations.

## Example

```tsx
const PopoverContent = React.forwardRef(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
  <PopoverPrimitive.Content ref={ref} className={cn('z-50 ...', className)} {...props} />
));
```
